        Analyze this image to extract detailed row data for score calculation.
        The image contains a table with columns: "Teacher Name", "Subject Name", "Subject Code", "Number of Columns".

        Task:
        1. Extract EVERY data row (exclude "Total" summary rows).
        2. Identify the "Teacher Name" for each row. Note that the Teacher Name cell might be merged vertically; apply the name to all relevant rows.
        3. Match the Teacher Name to the provided "Standard Name List".

        Standard Name List:
        ${referenceNames}

        Return a JSON array of objects with these fields:
        - "originalName": The exact name found in the image.
        - "standardName": The matched name from the Standard Name List (or null if no match).
        - "subjectCode": The Subject Code.
        - "count": The Number of Columns (as a number).
      `;

      const response = await ai.models.generateContent({
        model: 'gemini-2.5-flash',
        contents: {
          parts: [
            {
              inlineData: {
                mimeType: file.type,
                data: base64Data
              }
            },
            { text: prompt }
          ]
        },
        config: {
          responseMimeType: "application/json"
        }
      });

      const responseText = response.text;
      if (!responseText) throw new Error("No data returned from model.");

      const data = JSON.parse(responseText);

      let rows: any[] = [];
      if (Array.isArray(data)) {
        rows = data;
      } else if (typeof data === 'object' && data !== null) {
        const key = Object.keys(data).find(k => Array.isArray(data[k]));
        if (key) {
          rows = data[key];
        } else {
          rows = [data];
        }
      }

      // --- Processing Algorithm ---

      // 1. Build a map of Subject Code -> Set of Teachers to find shared subjects
      // We look at ALL rows to see which codes are taught by more than one person.
      const codeToTeachers = new Map<string, Set<string>>();

      rows.forEach(row => {
          // Identify teacher by standard name if possible, else original name
          const teacherId = row.standardName || row.originalName;
          const code = row.subjectCode ? String(row.subjectCode).trim().toUpperCase() : "";

          if (code && teacherId) {
             if (!codeToTeachers.has(code)) {
                 codeToTeachers.set(code, new Set());
             }
             codeToTeachers.get(code)?.add(teacherId);
